 /*
- * Minimal polled SWEET keys. Call once after the scheduler is running.
- * See hw-report.md: volume-up is PM6150L SID 4, NOT PM6150 SID 0.
- * PMIC access is READ ONLY: the sole MMIO write issues EXT_READL on an
- * observer channel. No PMIC config, IRQ acknowledge or reset writes exist.
+ * Moto G05 (MT6768 "lamu") hardware keys, polled; read-only access.
+ *
+ *  - Power: MT6358 PMIC TOPSTATUS (0x28) through the PMIC wrapper (pwrap @
+ *    0x1000d000, WACS2 channel). The key is down while PWRKEY_DEB (bit 0) reads 0.
+ *  - Volume: MediaTek keypad controller (kp @ 0x10010000). KP_MEM1..5 hold one bit
+ *    per hardware key, 0 = pressed. Android's DT maps hw key 0 to KEY_VOLUMEUP
+ *    and hw key 17 (KPD "reset key") to KEY_VOLUMEDOWN.
+ *
+ * Linux has already set everything up and left the clocks on. Nothing is
+ * written except the WACS2 read command and VLDCLR, exactly like the Linux
+ * pmic-wrap driver does for a read. All raw values are logged when they
+ * change, so the first run on the phone shows which bit is which key.
+ * Boot-args: sweetkeys=0 (off), sweetkeydelay=<s>, sweetkeypwr=<bit>,
+ * sweetkeyup=<hw key>, sweetkeydn=<hw key>.
  */
